# Linear — QA pass automation (board resolved)

## Default (Claude Extension + humans)

After a **pass**, run from **repo root**:

```bash
npm run qa:result -- --issue=<MIN-XX> --status=pass --result-file=<path-to-template-b.md>
```

That script uses the **Linear GraphQL API** with `LINEAR_API_KEY` (same backend an in-editor **Linear MCP** tool would call): it sets `qa:passed`, posts the comment, and **`issueUpdate`s the workflow `stateId` to the team’s first `type: completed` state** (Done). No separate MCP “mark resolved” step is required when this command succeeds.

- **`--no-resolve`** — set only labels + comment; do **not** change workflow state (rare; e.g. process requires Done only after merge).

## Linear MCP in Cursor chats

Use **Linear MCP** for interactive reads (issue details, search, comments) when helpful. For **recording a pass**, prefer **`npm run qa:result`** so behavior matches CI/docs and you do not double-apply state if both MCP and the script run.

## Fail / blocked

`--status=fail` or `blocked` updates `qa:*` labels (and optional comment) only — **no** automatic move to completed.
